107:  * - [default](https://github.com/markdown-it/markdown-it/blob/master/lib/presets/default.js) -
108:  *   similar to GFM, used when no preset name given. Enables all available rules,
109:  *   but still without html, typographer & autolinker.
110:  * - ["zero"](https://github.com/markdown-it/markdown-it/blob/master/lib/presets/zero.js) -
111:  *   all rules disabled. Useful to quickly setup your config via `.enable()`.
112:  *   For example, when you need only `bold` and `italic` markup and nothing else.
113:  *
